values ('f2a3b4c5-6d7e-4f22-9b12-2c3d4e5f6a22', 'acting-ii', 'Acting II', 'Acting II develops the actor''s craft through sustained scene study, character development, partner responsiveness, and rehearsal process. Building on Acting I, students learn to analyze scripts for playable action, build specific characters, pursue objectives through obstacles, work truthfully moment to moment, and present contemporary realist scenes with vocal, physical, emotional, and relational clarity. The course prepares students for Acting III, period/style work, auditions, production practicum, directing collaboration, and more advanced performance contexts.');

